{
  "$comment": "TASK-1038 R6 / TASK-1036 OD-23, OD-24, OD-33 (README §8.7, §10.3), frozen by lane F2 (TASK-1038 protocol-v2.md) — run protocol v2: ONE envelope `{ seq, runId, type, ts, nodeId?, data }` for SSE and WS. `header` / `query` select it (`x-hope-run-protocol: 2` or `?protocol=2`). `visibility` is the TYPE-level public/admin split; an `output.data` with `data.visibility: \"admin\"` is admin-only too (event-level audience). `nodeScope`: `required` / `optional` (transcripts sourced by the consultation session) / `forbidden`; an agent run's step nodeId is `agentRunNodeId`. `errorMessages` / `errorFallbackMessage`: `error.message` must be the fixed label of `error.code`; free text only in `error.detail` (never on the public plane). `examples` is one VALID event per type (plus extra shapes); each passes `runEventProblems` with the entry's `runKind` / `plane` when given. `invalid` entries each produce at least one problem containing `problem`. `sse` pins exact frame bytes (`event:`, `id: <seq>`, `data: <compact JSON of the whole envelope, keys in envelope order>`, blank line). `sequencer` is the ONE append script every producer uses (KEYS, stored field order, MAXLEN, closed error, terminal types, the Lua bytes); `stored` pins an append's EVAL arguments (`command`) and the resulting stream entry (`entry`, with the seq the script assigned) and the envelope it reads back as (`event`). `run.completed.data.result` is EXACTLY `{ kind: \"inline\", value }` or `{ kind: \"ref\", bucket, key, sizeBytes, sha256 }`. TypeScript: `packages/async-contract/src/__tests__/run-protocol.test.ts`; the Python mirror (wave B, B1) must read this file too.",
